libpdfium for Debian
------------------------

This package provides a Debian-compatible build of PDFium, Google's
high-performance PDF rendering library, adapted via an independently
maintained CMake-based build system originally developed by Olexiy Khokhlov
and contributors.

### Packaging rationale

Google's official PDFium build system is Chromium-centric and incompatible
with standard Debian workflows. This package uses a modern CMake-based port,
making it far more maintainable and compliant with Debian Policy and
best practices.

### Upstream source

The source used for this package is from:

  https://github.com/OlexiyKhokhlov/pdfium

While not the "official" upstream maintained by Google, this repository
tracks upstream PDFium releases and provides a clean, CMake-first build
layer more suited for integration with Linux distributions.

### Modifications

Several Debian-specific changes were made:

- **CMake minimum version lowered** via quilt patch to allow building with
  CMake 3.28, the current version in Debian stable.
- **Quilt patch series** manages compatibility and minor adjustments for
  packaging.
- **Clean split of runtime (`libpdfium20250629`) and development (`libpdfium-dev`) packages**, following standard naming and policy.

### Attribution and upstream credit

Though this packaging work was created independently, it builds upon the
efforts of:

- The upstream PDFium project (BSD-3-Clause), maintained by Google
- Olexiy Khokhlov’s CMake integration project
- Over 30 additional contributors to the CMake-based PDFium port

Redistributors are kindly encouraged (though not required) to acknowledge
those contributors when distributing this packaging.

### Snapshot versioning

This package tracks a specific upstream snapshot. The version string format
is:

    <YYYYMMDD>-1

For this build:

    20250629-1

This allows packaging of upstream revisions without waiting for formal
releases.

### Long-term goals

If there is community interest, this packaging could serve as a base for
eventual inclusion in the official Debian archive. At present, it is hosted
via an unofficial APT repository (see https://apt.valkyrianlabs.com).

